A small town is not a place. It is a group of people.

There are many ways to list a town in one's mind. They can be:

An actual place;

A fictional place;

A place in a dream;

A place in a story.

The first three of these methods are easy to understand. The last two are not so easy.

A small town can be a place in a book. It can be a place in a story. It can be a place in a dream. It can be in a nightmare.

